import{mJ}from"/$bunfs/root/chunk-4mwfrptf.js";var c8="SearchMcpRegistry",Dxs="Search the MCP connector registry by keyword to discover connectors that might help complete the task.",Lxs=`Search the MCP connector registry by keyword. Call this when connecting to an MCP server might help complete the task \u2014 whether or not the user named a specific product.

Named-product examples:
- "check my Asana tasks" \u2192 keywords ["asana", "tasks", "todo"]
- "find issues in Jira" \u2192 keywords ["jira", "issues"]

Intent-based examples (no product named):
- "help me manage my tasks" \u2192 keywords ["tasks", "todo", "project management"]
- "pull up the design mockups" \u2192 keywords ["design", "figma", "mockup"]

Returns a ranked list with directoryUuid, name, description, sample tool names, installState (org-level), and enabledInChat (this session). Results include the org's custom connectors (ones the org configured that are not in the public directory) when they match the keywords. enabledInChat: false means the connector's tools are not loaded in this session; the field does not say why. ${mJ} takes a result's directoryUuid whatever its installState is, not only that of a connector that is not installed. The user can also check a connector, and its tool permissions, in their claude.ai connector settings. Do not name a setting for this chat alone; there may be none. ${c8} does not itself connect anything.`;
