sources must lie under the working directory or your scratchpad directory (as your system prompt names it).`:'Supporting files to publish alongside the page. Map form {"published/path": "source/path" | {from, contentType} | null} publishes each source at the key (what the HTML references); when updating an existing artifact, files left out of the map are kept and null removes that path. List form publishes each file at its own spelling. Sources must lie under the working directory or your scratchpad directory (as your system prompt names it).')+nUs),root:o().min(1).max(1024).optional().describe(`Base directory that relative SOURCE paths resolve against (like a bundler root) \u2014 saves retyping a long build prefix. ${d?"Never changes the published path of a `files` entry":"Never changes published paths"}. Relative to the working directory, or absolute within it or your scratchpad directory (so files fetched or built there publish without copying). Requires \`files\`${d?" \u2014 except for an Artifact made from an Artifact type (or being created from one), where it may stand alone: a data `file_path` is then served at its path relative to `root`, unless a `files` map entry states its served path. Send it with every such publish, set to the folder that holds the Artifact's files at their served paths":""}.`)},limit:k().int().min(1).max(C7).optional().describe(`list only: maximum artifacts to return (default ${uke}).`),page_token:o().max(8192).optional().describe("list only: the `next_page_token` a listing of the same scope gave, to list the artifacts after it."),scope:B(EGn).optional().describe("list only: 'mine' (default) lists artifacts the user owns; 'shared' lists artifacts other people shared with the user; 'all' lists both. Rows are labeled (mine)/(shared) whenever scope is not 'mine'."+(v?" With `type` or `type_url` (the Artifacts made from a type) the default is 'all': the user's own, their organization's, and ones shared with them.":"")),title:o().optional()