n `(active) *` row. Unless you ran it and saw no such row, or a call failed (Errors, below), don't bring up signing in, nor a key unless it is the right answer, not even beside code they will run later. If the block has one:"],["get a short-lived token with `ant auth print-credentials --access-token` and send it as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` **plus**","send `Authorization: Bearer $(ant auth print-credentials --access-token)` (short-lived, and never printed this way; if the active row is `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, send `$ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`) **plus**"],["Only ask the user for a key if `ant auth status` reports no active credential source (or `ant` itself isn't installed). Suggest `ant auth login` as the first option - it stores a profile under `~/.config/anthropic/` that the SDKs read automatically - and an exported `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` as the alternative.",["**If it has none, offer the `ant` sign-in first and an API key second** (no browser on this machine: read that bullet first). `ant auth login` opens a browser tab where the user signs in to the Claude Console and picks a workspace; API usage is billed to the Console organization, never to a claude.ai plan. It saves tokens under `~/.config/anthropic/`, creates no API key and adds no credits. In Claude Code, ask the user to type `! ant auth login` at the prompt (`!` runs it outside the sandbox), or to run it in a terminal of their own; don't run it yourself unless they ask. Tell them first that this needs a Console account, separate from claude.ai (if they have none, that tab lets them create one), to approve in the tab and to paste nothing here: the link it prints and its `paste the code here` work only in a terminal of their own. Then make one real call (`ant models list` is free, or run their code) before you say it works: `ant auth status` sends no request. Tell them too that Claude Code keeps its own `/login`; if that stops working, Claude Code falls back to this sign-in and bills the API organization.","","- **A claude.ai plan:** Max, Ultra and Team include monthly API credits, which the user (on Team, an owner) claims on claude.ai: `shared/api-sign-in.md`. You can't see whether they can, so promise none. Free, Pro and Enterprise include none. If the user names their plan, tell them which; never say that Max, Ultra or Team doesn't cover the API. If they name none, don't bring plans up unless a call fails for credits.","- **`ant` is missing, or is Apache Ant** (it answers about `build.xml`): the sign-in still comes first. Offer to install Anthropic's CLI: `brew install anthropics/tap/ant` (macOS), `go install github.com/anthropics/anthropic-cli/v2/cmd/ant@latest` (with Go), or on Linux/WSL the command at `https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/cli-sdks-libraries/cli/quickstart` (it uses `sudo`, so they run it; it names a release, so never make one up). Beside Apache Ant, never use the bare name: each command you run, and each you give them (the login too), takes the full path of Anthropic's `ant`, as in `! $(go env GOPATH)/bin/ant auth login` after `go install`; `which -a ant` lists every `ant` on `PATH`.","- **A key is the right answer** when one already works (leave it alone), when the code will run elsewhere (a deploy target, CI, a server: a key in that platform's secret store, or Workload Identity Federation), or when a tool reads only `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. The user creates it in the Console and sets it themselves.","- **Errors:** a 401 or `invalid_grant` on a sign-in that used to work means it has run out: sign in again the same way. `credit balance is too low` means that organization has no credits the call can use. They buy some under Billing in the Console. Max, Ultra and Team plans include monthly API credits, claimed on claude.ai (`shared/api-sign-in.md`). If they claimed those for another organization, they sign in to it under a new profile (`! ant auth login --profile <name>`; a plain login keeps the organization). Otherwise signing in again, or a key for that organization, won't help.","- **No browser on this machine:** over SSH they run `ant auth login --no-browser` in a terminal of their own on that host (`!` and your own commands get no keyboard input). Where they have only this chat (Claude Code on the web, `CLAUDE_CODE_REMOTE=true`), don't start a login: they set `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in the settings of a cloud environment only they use, then start a new session.","- **Never** take a login code, a key or a token through this chat. Never open, print or copy anything in the sign-in store's `credentials/` folder, or run `ant auth print-credentials` with no flag (that prints the refresh token); use `--access-token` or `--env` only inside `$(...)` in the command that needs it, never into a file. `ant auth status` already gives the account, expiry and scopes."].join(`
